## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/monotorgb.html
- Summary (EN): Converts a mono layer, VDB or attribute to RGB by passing its values through a colour ramp. It can apply input and output scaling and controls how values outside the input range are handled.
- Résumé (FR) : Fait passer une valeur mono par une rampe de couleurs pour obtenir du RGB, avec mise à l'échelle d'entrée et de sortie et gestion des valeurs hors plage par pincement ou répétition.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the mono layer, VDB or attribute to convert", "ramp (optional): an RGB layer sampled along a horizontal line through the centre of the image; use it instead of the Ramp parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source accepts", "Compute Range: sets Input Min and Input Max to the source minimum and maximum", "Input Min / Input Max: source values mapped to the start and end of the ramp", "Output Min / Output Max: shift and scale the ramp's black and white points before it is applied", "Scale by Value: multiplies the ramp colour by the normalised input value, so output can keep brightening outside the ramped range", "Outside Range: Clamp at End pins out-of-range values to the ramp ends; Repeat cycles the ramp colours", "Ramp: the RGB ramp; the left side corresponds to Input Min and the right side to Input Max"]

- Caveats: ["The page includes no explicit warning.", "The page suggests that if no ramping or clamping is needed, a mono layer can be wired directly into the destination node for an implicit RGB conversion."]

